[{:seon.task/name "a-pulls-cost-is-a-function-of-its-input"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-10 by the test session (`seon.cost-test/measure-unit :db/pull-attr 30`: a 2-attribute ``d/pull`` less a 1-attribute pull on one in-memory db): 2,774 ticks and 8,560 B alone in a process; 2,590 and 7,488 after nine other test namespaces ran; 1,976 and 6,768 in a forked child after one warm call. Ticks and bytes move 13-28% with what ran earlier in the process, so a cost proof on the pull path measures its shard's history. Ruled out by reading: Jolt's per-call-site protocol caches (built only with --opt, which bin/build does not pass) and the node cache (an in-memory index is never written). Candidates, each with the one measurement that decides it: the depth of the dynamic-binding stack (a read of a bound var walks it, once an attribute: measure inside a fresh binding of ``datahike.index.interface/*reads*``); Datahike's schema cache, shared by every store of the process (reset ``datahike.schema-cache/schema-meta-cache`` first); where the call sits on its Chez stack segment (a segment overflow allocates a counted continuation: measure at 0, 50 and 200 nested calls). None explains the same pull allocating 1 KB less after other namespaces ran. Next step: a per-function self-bytes profile of the unit, fresh and after the nine namespaces, diffed. Until fixed, the unit table measures in a fresh process."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-pull-of-an-attribute-records-its-slice"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by context 2026-11-14 building the reaction core (seon.ratom/a-reaction-is-tracked-by-the-stores-recorder) [M]: a pull of one attribute, (d/pull db [:a] e), records [:e e] as well as [:ea e a], because resolve-pull-eid checks that e exists with (first (dbi/datoms db :eavt [eid])) under the recorder; a pattern of more than one attribute records [:e e] too, from entity-datoms' one :eavt range read. So a reaction or page component that pulled one slice of an entity reruns on a commit to any other attribute of it (red when the proof seon.ratom-test/a-reaction-reruns-on-a-commit-touching-a-key-it-read reads by pull). Every page component reads by pull, so this is the grain of the whole page. The fix is the recorder's, in the one place: a pull records what it kept, [:ea e a] for each attribute of its pattern (an absent one included, so its first value reaches it), and the existence probe records no wider key than the attributes read; the one :eavt range read stays (cost unchanged). Proof: a pull of [:a :b] of e is reached by a datom of e's :a or :b and not of e's :c. Estimate (written first, 2026-11-14): n = entities pulled, k = the pattern's forward attributes; the :eavt range is still read once (O(datoms of e), unchanged), plus k recorded ranges per entity, each two bound datoms and a conj, ~200 ticks and ~150 B, only while recording; off the recorder, one dynamic-var read per entity."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.reads-test/a-pull-records-the-attributes-it-read}}
